        "content": "<p>I'm currently reading Introduction to convex geometry by W.A. Coppel, and I'd like to formalize the notion of an Alignment from page 6. Here's what I have so far:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- An alignment on `X`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alignment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- A predicate saying that a set is an open set. Use `IsConvex` in the root namespace instead. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConvex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The set representing the whole space is an convex set.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Use `isConvex_univ` in the root namespace instead. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isConvex_univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConvex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The intersection of any family of convex sets is a convex set. Use</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    `IsConvex.sInter` instead. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isConvex_sInter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConvex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConvex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⋂₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The union of a non-empty indexed family of convex sets totally ordered by inclusion is a</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  convex set. Use `isConvex_sUnion` in the root namespace instead. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isConvex_sUnion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Total</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConvex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⋃₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, I don't understand how to formalize the last requirement that the union of any totally ordered family of convex sets is itself convex. The above gives the error \"failed to synthesize instance of type class HasSubset ↑s.\" How do I fix this? And more generally, what's the best way to formalize this requirement?</p>",
        "id": 611571537,
        "sender_full_name": "Lucas Allen",
        "timestamp": 1784514057
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can write <code>fun (a : Set X) b ↦ a ∈ s → b ∈ s → a ⊆ b</code> instead</p>",
        "id": 611647686,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1784548537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>or <code>fun (a : s) b ↦ a.1 ⊆ b.1</code>. The point is that <code>a : ↑s</code> means <code>a</code> has type <code>{x : Set X // x ∈ s}</code>, which does not have this HasSubset instance.</p>",
        "id": 611648014,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1784548672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That works, thank you.</p>",
        "id": 611773745,
        "sender_full_name": "Lucas Allen",
        "timestamp": 1784588171
    }
]